  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, 0.639 acc) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, and RNA is the dominant signal (0.485 alone vs 0.208 image-only). However, the RNA encoder axis is completely unexplored in the multimodal setting—we have only tested a linear PCA projection. Question: config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is a single-variable change from config_019, swapping PCA for a learned variational autoencoder representation. This directly tests whether a non-linear, biologically-informed RNA representation can improve over PCA in the best-known configuration. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It tests the highest-leverage unexplored axis—improving the dominant modality's representation has the largest potential upside. (2) It is a controlled comparison (only RNA encoder changes), so any performance shift is cleanly attributable to the encoder. (3) The result will determine whether to invest further in learned RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) or confirm PCA is sufficient, shaping all subsequent experiments. (4) Compared to filling the transformer+weighted cell (config_021), the RNA encoder question has greater uncertainty and greater potential impact given RNA's dominance."
}

